course: dictionary
lesson: 10898
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word virtue is a good example. It can mean goodness and right behaviour, or a good quality in a person, or a good point about something.
explain: «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage.» Here a virtue is one good quality. Honesty and courage are the examples, so the sentence is about good qualities in people.
explain: «The virtue of this bike is that it's light.» Here virtue means a good point or advantage. The words «of this bike» and the sentence about being light are the clues. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the good point of this bike is that it's light" still makes sense.
fact: Virtue means goodness and right behaviour.
fact: A virtue is a good quality in a person, such as honesty, kindness, patience or courage.
fact: «Patience is a virtue» is a proverb, a short saying that teaches a lesson about life.
fact: «By virtue of» is a formal phrase that means because of.
fact: Virtues are good habits, and vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty.
exercise: «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage.» What is a virtue in this sentence? | A bad habit, like greed | A kind of weather | A place to live | *A good quality, like honesty
exercise: «The virtue of this bike is that it's light.» What does virtue mean here? | A bad habit | *A good point or advantage | Goodness and right behaviour | A kind of bike
exercise: «By virtue of» is a formal phrase. What does it mean? | Before | Instead of | Even though | *Because of
test: What does the proverb «Patience is a virtue» teach us? | Patience never matters | Patience is a bad habit | Patience is a kind of weather | *Being patient is a good thing
test: Which word means a bad habit, such as greed or cruelty? | Courage | Honesty | *Vice | Virtue
exam: «Aristotle said good actions build virtues, like kindness and courage, that are part of a good, happy life.» In this sentence, what does virtues mean? | Bad habits such as greed | *Good qualities, like kindness and courage | Good points of a bike | Phrases that mean because of
